Z||000000||Gonzo_442||12-13-2000||10:14 PM||||my turn signals started acting funny recently.<P>when i turn them on (either direction) it starts blinking like normal, but after a few blinks it starts acting like it doesn't want to blink off or back on. i don't know if i'm explaining this well enough for you to understand it. it seems like they hesitate when going from on to off and off to on.<P>i checked the wiring, all the bulbs. connections are tight, bulbs are good. they work (sort of) so i assume the flasher unit is still okay.<P>anyone know whats going on?<BR>i'm thinking about replacing the flasher just to see if it solves the problem.<BR>thanks, any thoughts are appreciated.<P>------------------<BR>--<BR>g||||reg||5
Z||000001||kornholio||12-13-2000||10:20 PM||||I had this problem also.  I replaced the flasher and it was fine.  It's only a couple bucks anyway.||||reg||1
Z||000002||BAM-BAM||12-13-2000||11:22 PM||||   Gonzo, Also check for a loose ground wire. I had a similar problem that plagued me fo months. Then I desided to shotgun all the bulbs and found a ground wire hanging off on the left rear. Just a thought.<P> Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
